.TH ATERMINAL 1 "2026-11-06" "aterminal @PROJECT_VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
aterminal \- phosphor CRT terminal emulator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aterminal
.RB [ \-\-green | \-\-amber ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-sound | \-\-sound ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-crt ]
.RB [ \-\-bitmap ]
.br
.RB [ \-\-size
.IR WIDTH x HEIGHT ]
.RB [ \-\-width
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-height
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-text\-size
.IR N ]
.br
.RB [ \-\-colour
.BR green | amber ]
.RB [ \-\-fullscreen [ =true | =false ]| \-\-windowed ]
.br
.RB [ \-\-shell
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-e
.IR command ]
.RB [ \-c
.IR command ]
.RB [ \-\-demo ]
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B aterminal
is a native Linux terminal with the look of a phosphor CRT: green or amber
text, soft bloom, scanlines, a vignette, and optional AdLib\-style key sounds.
.PP
Twelve independent shell consoles live behind the F1\-F12 keys. Each one starts
its own pseudo\-terminal when first visited and keeps running in the background.
.PP
.B aterminal
implements a practical VT100/ANSI subset with Unicode extensions, not complete
xterm compatibility. See
.B BUGS
before using it with applications that depend on advanced terminal features.
.PP
The window title shows the console and its size in characters, such as
.BR "aterminal / F1 / 80x25" .
.SH OPTIONS
Options that take a value accept either
.BI \-\-flag= value
or
.BI \-\-flag " value\fR."
Command\-line choices override saved preferences. If a setting appears more
than once, the last one wins.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show flags and keyboard shortcuts, then exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-size " WIDTH" x HEIGHT
Set the initial window size in pixels. The default is 1104x768.
.TP
.BI \-\-width " N\fR, " \-\-height " N"
Set the dimensions separately. Width is 400\-4096 and height is 280\-2160.
.TP
.BI \-\-text\-size " N"
Set the initial zoom level, 1\-5. The default is 2 when no preference is saved.
.TP
.BR \-\-colour " " green | amber ", " \-\-color " " green | amber
Choose the phosphor colour.
.TP
.BR \-\-green ", " \-\-amber
Short aliases for
.BR \-\-colour .
.TP
.BR \-\-fullscreen [ =true | =false | =1 | =0 ]
Start in desktop fullscreen, or windowed if the value is false.
.TP
.B \-\-windowed
Start windowed.
.TP
.BR \-\-sound ", " \-\-no\-sound
Enable or disable synthesized key clicks.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-crt
Disable bloom, scanlines, and the vignette.
.TP
.B \-\-bitmap
Use bitmap glyphs throughout instead of the mixed retro font.
.TP
.BI \-\-shell " path"
Select the shell executable. The path must be absolute.
.TP
.BI \-e " command\fR, " \-\-command " command"
Run
.I command
in the selected shell using
.BR \-c .
Quote it as one argument. Newly opened consoles run it too.
.TP
.BI \-c " command"
Run
.I command
at startup, then continue in an interactive shell. It runs once, in the first
console only, and cannot be combined with
.B \-e
or
.BR \-\-demo .
Startup files run for the interactive shell, not for
.IR command ,
so aliases are not available to it.
.TP
.B \-\-demo
Display the built\-in font and terminal demonstration, then open a shell.
.TP
.B \-\-self\-test
Run the SDL interaction checks without loading or saving preferences.
.TP
.BI \-\-frames " N"
Exit after
.I N
event\-loop iterations, 1\-1000000. This is not a duration in seconds.
.TP
.BI \-\-screenshot " path"
Save the final rendered display as a PNG when the application exits.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B F1\-F12
Switch to that console, creating it on first use. These keys are not forwarded
to applications.
.TP
.BR + ", " \-
Increase or decrease the text size.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+Plus\fR, \fBCtrl+Shift+Minus
Send a literal
.B +
or
.B \-
to the shell.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+A\fR, \fBCtrl+Shift+G
Select amber or green phosphor.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+S
Toggle key sounds.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+R
Toggle CRT effects.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+B
Toggle all\-bitmap font mode.
.TP
.B Alt+Enter\fR, \fBCtrl+Shift+F
Toggle fullscreen.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+P\fR, right click
Open or close terminal setup. Escape also closes it.
.TP
Mouse drag
Select text. A single click clears the selection.
.TP
.B Ctrl+C
Copy the selected text and clear the selection, or send an interrupt when
nothing is selected.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+C
Copy the selected text without sending an interrupt.
.TP
.B Ctrl+V\fR, \fBCtrl+Shift+V\fR, \fBShift+Insert\fR, middle click
Paste.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Z\fR, \fBCtrl+Y
Forward to the shell or application.
.TP
.B Shift+PageUp\fR, \fBShift+PageDown\fR, mouse wheel
Move through the scrollback.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+Enter
Restart the current shell after it exits.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SHELL
The shell to start, unless
.B \-\-shell
is given. If it is unset,
.B /bin/sh
is used.
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
Base directory for the preferences file.
.TP
.BR TERM ", " COLORTERM
Set to
.B xterm\-256color
and
.B truecolor
for child processes.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ${XDG_DATA_HOME:\-$HOME/.local/share}/ross\-newman/aterminal/preferences
Colour, sound, CRT effects, font mode, and text zoom, saved on normal exit.
Remove this file while
.B aterminal
is closed to reset them.
.TP
.I share/aterminal/unifont.hex
Unicode font data, located relative to the installed executable.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal exit.
.TP
.B 1
An option was invalid, or startup failed.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
.B aterminal \-\-colour=amber \-\-size=1280x800 \-\-text\-size=3
.B aterminal \-\-green \-\-fullscreen \-\-no\-sound
.B aterminal \-\-shell /bin/bash \-e htop
.fi
.SH BUGS
.B aterminal
advertises
.B xterm\-256color
but does not implement every xterm sequence. Mouse reporting, sixel graphics,
OSC clipboard access, custom tab stops, and DEC double\-height text are not
implemented. Emoji are monochrome, and complex\-script shaping and bidirectional
layout are not implemented.
.PP
Sessions are not restored across launches. Closing the window terminates its
shells.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bash (1),
.BR tmux (1),
.BR xterm (1)
